module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheaf.Subscheme
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Modules.Sheaf
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Modules.Invertible

/-!
# The zero scheme of a section of an invertible module

Let `L` be an invertible module on a scheme `X` and let `s ∈ Γ(X, L)` be a global section. On an
affine open `U` the section `s` spans a submodule of `Γ(L, U)`, and applying every linear
functional `Γ(L, U) →ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U)` to it produces an ideal of `Γ(X, U)`: the ideal
generated by the "coordinates of `s`". For an invertible module the functionals are the sections
of the inverse tensor power, so this ideal is the image of the evaluation map
`L^{⊗ -1} ⟶ 𝒪_X` at `s`. The closed subscheme it cuts out is the *zero scheme* `Z(s)` of `s`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme` — the quasi-coherent ideal sheaf of the zero scheme; its closed
  subscheme and closed immersion are `zeroScheme.subscheme` and `zeroScheme.subschemeι`.

## Implementation notes

`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals` produces the largest quasi-coherent ideal
sheaf contained in a prescribed affine-local family of ideals, so the definition below needs no
compatibility proof. Identifying `(zeroScheme X L s).ideal U` with the prescribed ideal on *every*
affine open — the other half of Stacks 02OQ — is a separate statement, proved as
`Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme_ideal` in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.ZeroSchemePullback.ZeroSchemeIdeal`. It needs that the
prescribed family is already compatible with restriction to basic opens, which in turn needs that
an invertible module is finite locally free of rank one (Stacks 0B8M, proved as
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_iff_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one_algebraicGeometry`) and that
its sections localize (Stacks 01P7, proved as
`AlgebraicGeometry.isLocalizedModule_restriction_basicOpen_of_qcqs`). The tag's covering set is
therefore the definition below together with that identification.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OQ)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory

universe u

namespace Stacks.Divisors

/-- **Stacks 02OQ.** The quasi-coherent ideal sheaf cutting out the zero scheme of a global
section `s` of an invertible module `L` on `X`: on an affine open `U` it is generated by the
values `φ (s|_U)` of the `Γ(X, U)`-linear functionals `φ` on `Γ(L, U)`. The closed subscheme
itself is `(zeroScheme X L s).subscheme`, with closed immersion
`(zeroScheme X L s).subschemeι`. -/
@[stacks 02OQ "the closed subscheme construction"]
noncomputable abbrev zeroScheme (X : Scheme.{u}) (L : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property L]
    (s : Γ(L, ⊤)) : X.IdealSheafData :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdeals (fun U =>
    Ideal.span {a : Γ(X, U.1) | ∃ φ : Γ(L, U.1) →ₗ[Γ(X, U.1)] Γ(X, U.1),
      a = φ (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op s)})

end Stacks.Divisors

end
